		text: `# kdx-avatar > **Problem thesis (required):** kdx-avatar is a host-local **interface adapter** that turns a real webcam feed into a live digital avatar stream (VRM puppet via SnekStudio) and exposes it as a stable video interface for consumers (virtual camera, OBS). The core pain is that existing avatar apps are not **service-shaped**: they do not guarantee continuous valid video on failure, do not keep a control plane alive when the puppet dies, and do not coordinate device policy with sibling tools on the same machine. This repo solves that with a two-layer failover model — blank frames on the export path, full service operability on the control path — while treating SnekStudio as a collaboration partner rather than a fork target.`,
