		text: `### P1 — No automated enforcement of prepaid shower access - **Who hurts:** Truck-stop staff and truckers using paid shower facilities; operators who previously tracked usage on paper or by memory. - **Pain today:** Cards could be reused beyond paid limits, stale cards stayed valid indefinitely, and there was no reliable way to block inactive or expired credentials at the physical door. - **How this repo answers:** An async RFID polling loop ( in ) reads card UIDs every 500 ms and calls in . Validation runs in order: account exists → → not passed → . On grant: green LED, single beep, relay open for 5 seconds, one credit deducted, immutable access log written. On deny: red LED, differentiated buzzer pattern (3 beeps for out-of-credits, 1 long beep otherwise), reason recorded ( , , , ). - **Out of scope:** Payment processing, multi-door zones, anti-passback, card-cloning detection, cloud billing integration.`,
